<title>BRAZIL: SAO PAULO FIRMS SACK 9,823 WORKERS IN JULY.</title>
<headline>SAO PAULO FIRMS SACK 9,823 WORKERS IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private firms in Sao Paulo state laid off 9,823 workers in July, against 4,278 in June, Sao Paulo State Industries Federation (Fiesp) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Last month, 29 out of 47 sectors included in the survey sacked personnel, 15 hired new employees and three maintained their staff unchanged, it said.</p>
<p>In the last 12 months, Sao Paulo firms have sacked 108,080 employees. So far this year, the firms have laid off 50,434 workers, it added.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
